{"kind":"request","text":"Security: the bounded-JSONata subset gate is bypassable at main head 055687c. validateJSONataSource (internal/profile/compiler.go:418) is pure source-TEXT lexing and is blind to two constructs, both reproduced end-to-end (gate admits AND the pinned v206 evaluator compiles+executes) by a probe test run at 055687c:\n\nH-NEW-1 — the apply operator ~\u003e invokes any unary builtin with NO \"$name(\", so the jsonataCallRE allowlist (which only fires on $name-with-paren) never sees it. Verified admitted+executed: `event ~\u003e $keys`, `event ~\u003e $spread`, `event ~\u003e $reverse`, `[\"b\",\"a\"] ~\u003e $sort`, `\"x\" ~\u003e $base64encode`. $keys/$spread defeat the deliberate object-wildcard exclusion, giving a telemetry-exfil path (enumerate/serialize arbitrary record structure a fold was never meant to read).\n\nH-NEW-2 — λ is a Unicode synonym for function, but jsonataLambdaRE (compiler.go:40) is ASCII-only (\\bfunction\\s*\\(). Verified admitted+executed: `(\"x\" ~\u003e λ($s){$s \u0026 $s} ~\u003e λ($s){$s \u0026 $s})` yields \"xxxx\". Arbitrary user lambdas plus recursion via ~\u003e become expressible, and because fold evaluation has NO step or allocation budget (only SetMaxDepth/SetMaxRange/SetMaxTime; the 250ms wall time is a machine-dependent safety net, not a deterministic bound — types.go), the \u0026 string-doubling gives geometric growth: a small program can churn multi-GB per OTLP event and break projection isolation. This is the same class as the previously-filed \u0026/:=-doubling finding, now reachable through lambdas too.\n\nRoot cause (shared with the prior confinement findings): the subset is enforced by regex/substring lexing of source text, which is structurally blind to ~\u003e, λ, and operator-driven growth. DURABLE FIX: validate the COMPILED AST, not the source text — the evaluator exposes Expression.AST() (jsonata v206 jsonata.go:549). Reject apply/lambda/transform nodes and any function reference (not just $name( calls) whose name is outside the allowlist; keep the text regexes only as defense-in-depth. This closes ~\u003e, λ, and any other surface-syntax evasion in one place. Whatever the fix, it changes the admitted language, so RuntimeID (internal/profile/types.go:11) must bump. Evidence: apply_probe_test.go attached (drop into internal/profile, `go test -run TestApplyOperatorAndLambdaSynonymBypassSubsetGate -v` — all six constructs log ADMITTED + EXECUTED at 055687c).\n\nFollow the usual flow: fix on a branch, add a test that asserts these constructs are now REFUSED by the gate, bump RuntimeID, publish exact-head artifacts, request checker review.","body":{"conditions":"At an exact reviewed head: the JSONata subset gate refuses (a) apply-operator invocation of any function outside the allowlist (e.g. record ~\u003e $keys / $spread / $sort / $base64encode) and (b) the Unicode lambda synonym λ, ideally by validating the compiled AST rather than source text; a regression test asserts these constructs are rejected; RuntimeID is bumped to reflect the narrowed admitted language; the full test/race/vet/demo battery passes; builder publishes exact-head artifacts for the changed paths and files a review request to checker, and a checker review verdict is filed on that head.","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}